  "reconstructibility": 1,
  "reason": "The records establish the exact AlCoCrFeNi2.1 alloy's coupled FCC/L12–B2 lamellar structure and room-temperature mechanical properties (R8, R16), while other HEA studies show that annealing temperature can alter ordering, decomposition, precipitation, and deformation behavior (R2, R5, R11, R14, R19, R20). They therefore suggest studying temperature-dependent aging of the eutectic alloy. However, none identifies the specific 600–750 °C ductile-brittle-ductile sequence, maximization of near-stoichiometric L12 order and jagged phase boundaries at 600 °C, or the combined APBE/modulus–cross-slip–planar-slip and boundary-tip stress-concentration mechanism. Reconstructing those details would require substantial additional insight and experiments."
